{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to flag something important from the backend side. While tracing an unrelated SDK issue yesterday, I confirmed that three named legacy consumers can only read the current Avro envelope. This means the migration needs an Avro compatibility gateway and exactly 21 days of dual publishing. I haven't updated the RFC yet to reflect this, but it directly impacts the direct protobuf publishing proposal — we can't simply switch to direct protobuf without an Avro compatibility layer for those consumers during the transition."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thanks everyone for getting the specifics out. To summarize the privacy implications: with the tokenization requirement I flagged, the 'direct protobuf publishing' proposal needs to be modified so that events are tokenized before entering the bus. That's non-negotiable for privacy sign-off given the precise location data in the payloads. On the EU storage requirement, that also stands — the RFC must specify EU region storage, not the default US region. I'll file the privacy review record formally so it's captured in the system. Riley, once I've filed it, the privacy sign-off will be contingent on those two changes being reflected in the revised RFC: tokenization before the bus and EU region storage."}
```

{"type":"say","text":"Thanks, Nadia — that's a critical finding. The location data in activity payloads changes the picture significantly. Tokenization before entering the bus and EU-region storage both sound like hard requirements for privacy sign-off, and they directly conflict with two elements of the current draft RFC (unrestricted payload publishing and default US region storage). I'm noting that as a must-address before approval.

Maya, before we get to your compatibility issue, let me make sure I have the privacy constraints straight: we need tokenization applied before events hit the bus, and storage must be EU region. Are there any additional privacy requirements beyond those two, or is that the full scope of what needs to change?

And Maya, please go ahead and walk us through your compatibility finding after that — I want to make sure we capture all the blockers before we discuss revisions."}

